man - display a manual page

SYNOPSIS
    man [section] topic

DESCRIPTION
    Display the named page from /usr/share/man. With no section,
    search sections 1, 2 and 5 in that order.

    When standard input and output are the foreground console, man
    opens a pager. The bottom line shows the current range of display
    lines. The size is read from the console when the pager opens.
    If either descriptor is redirected, man writes the page
    as plain text.

PAGER COMMANDS
    Down, j, Enter      Move down one line.
    Up, k              Move up one line.
    Page Down, Space   Move forward one screen.
    Page Up, b         Move back one screen.
    Home, g            Go to the start.
    End, G             Go to the end.
    Ctrl+L             Redraw the screen.
    q                  Return to the shell.

    Ctrl+Z suspends the pager. Use fg to resume at the same place.

FILES
    /usr/share/man/topic.section    Installed manual page.

EXAMPLES
    man ls
    man 2 execve
    man ls | grep SYNOPSIS

EXIT STATUS
    The exit status is 0 on success, 1 if the page cannot be opened or
    displayed, or 2 for invalid usage.

SEE ALSO
    apropos(1), less(1), sh(1), stty(1), ttyctl(2)
